    "description": "As a Brand Manager or Ops user, I want to see whether a deal reached the CMS and force a re-send when it did not.\n\n* CMS_Sync_Status__c picklist (Not Published / Pending / Synced / Failed / Retrying)\n\n* CMS_Sync_Note__c Long Text Area (2000) — most recent attempt's message\n\n* CMS_Last_Sync_Attempt\\__c, CMS_Last_Sync_Success_\\_c DateTime — lets Ops distinguish 'synced' from 'synced, but six days ago'\n\n* All grouped in the Ops section of the Deal record page\n\n* Field History Tracking enabled on CMS_Sync_Status__c so the pattern of failures over time is visible\n\n* The 'Sync with CMS' button calls the SAME invocable Apex as the automatic path — no duplicate code path\n\n* Button visible to Brand Manager and Ops only via dynamic action visibility; NEVER visible to reps\n\n* Repeated presses are safe; the CMS receives a normal update event\n\n* Automatic retry: three attempts with backoff before status is set to Failed\n\n* On failure the note contains HTTP status and response body, truncated to field length\n\n* Sync fields exist on Deal ONLY, not on Deal Link — publish is deal-scoped, links inherit their deal's sync state\n\n* List-view mass action supports bulk retry after a CMS outage\n\nEffort: 8-12h. Blocked by BUILD-66.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §4.4.",
